    "sha": "093b6fd86be2fd28887bcb9ba9008ac97019dc61",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDA5M2I2ZmQ4NmJlMmZkMjg4ODdiY2I5YmE5MDA4YWM5NzAxOWRjNjE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T13:33:38Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T13:33:38Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): judge radial rapids against the raw stock instead of standing the law down\n\nLaw (d) stood down for Mode::Radial (M5.2 F2): the column reading cannot\nsee a horizontal bore, so the kernel's traverse promise was trusted and a\ncross-drill rapid through uncut stock posted silently (#77's shape).\n\nRadial programs now get a solid reading (verify/rapids_radial.rs): the\nposed flute body, sampled under the modal pose rule, against the stock\nprism minus the kerf the earlier cuts swept. A rapid through stock reads\nRapidInStock and blocks the post; retracts up a just-drilled hole and peck\nchip breaks ride their own kerf and stay clean.\n\ndrilling_cross's 44 mm box fixture is a real #77 collision on main (the\napproach stops inside the raw box): the clean-document test runs on a\nbar-sized stock, and a new test pins that the box document never posts\nsilently.\n\nFixes #79\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
