  {
    "sha": "b8f1bad241d40811ab9f1989dfa498dce03cf995",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGI4ZjFiYWQyNDFkNDA4MTFhYjlmMTk4OWRmYTQ5OGRjZTAzY2Y5OTU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T14:07:05Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T14:07:05Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): radial rapid law - linear cost, fail closed, pinned edges\n\nPR #83 review fixes for the radial (cross-drill) rapid-in-stock law:\n\n- perf: the kerf list is built once in cut order with per-cylinder boxes;\n  each rapid takes only the earlier kerfs meeting its swept box (padded\n  by body + radius), newest first; discs whose box misses the stock\n  footprint box (or stand above the top) skip Region::contains; a disc\n  wholly inside one kerf cylinder is acquitted in one test; shared\n  interval ends are sampled once. 40-hole pecked radial program (debug):\n  ~9.5 s before (1 mm discs) -> ~0.25 s after (0.5 mm discs), pinned\n  by a 3 s wall-time bound.\n- fail closed by name: a non-finite stock top / Z tolerance or a tool\n  with no finite positive radius convicts every rapid (RapidInStock); a\n  rapid whose pose is no direction convicts itself instead of reading\n  as upright; a zero or non-finite flute length reads as a body one\n  tool diameter long.\n- docs: BODY_STEP is 0.5 mm, as the module doc says; the 16-sample rim's\n  ~0.019 r chord-sag bound is documented.\n- sim tests: past a drilled hole's bottom, tangential graze within /\n  beyond the gouge tolerance, diagonal retract half in the hole, the\n  non-finite context, the zero-direction pose, the zero/NaN flute, the\n  40-hole timing bound; the mill-mode twin asserts non-empty before .all().\n- app tests: radial tests move to drilling_cross_rapids.rs (fixtures to\n  tests/cross_support/, drilling_cross 565 -> 254 lines); new\n  deterministic a_station_hop_spliced_through_the_bar_is_named_and_the_post_refuses\n  (independent of the #77 planner); both tests post on a B-trunnion\n  mill-turn so the refusal must name the rapid, not the machine limits.\n\nRefs #79\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
